roughly one year after the initial  launch of its online RPG the crew  Ubisoft has now released the wilderun  expansion which like the original is  bursting with engaging wilderun fills  out the face game's cooperative  cross-country racing with motorcycles  monster trucks dragon drift builds new  licensed vehicles dynamic weather visual  upgrades throughout game wide physics  adjustments and a massive ongoing online  competition called the summit  unfortunately execution once again  undermines ambition while the handling  physics in general visuals have  undoubtedly improved they still haven't  caught up with other racing games like  the mechanically robust quartz ax when  the visually slick Need for Speed still  drifting Brad expects add even more  variety to the crews already impressive  collection of race types while the  monster trucks and the massive skatepark  arenas that come with them inject some  goofy fun in spite of all the new  content however many of the base game's  frustrations persist the UI is an  unintuitive mess the story is still  laughably bad and finding players to  join my crew frequently took longer than  it should have as a result the crew as a  whole remains a lackluster experience  even with its monster truck half pipes
 

